            <ArticleTitle>A novel iridoid from Torricellia angulata var intermedia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/14786410500463288</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new iridoid, named torricellate, was isolated from root bark of Torricellia angulata var intermedia, a Chinese folk medicinal plant used to treat bone fracture, tonsillitis and asthma. Its structure was elucidated by NMR, MS, IR and UV, and confirmed by X-ray diffraction studies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
